# Deploy a locally-built image to the k3s server

The cluster runs custom images with `imagePullPolicy: Never` and a bare image
name, so there is no registry: the image must be streamed to the node and
imported into k3s containerd by hand.

```bash
TAG=release.2026-08-20T12-50-18Z.1          # from scripts/build-image.sh
IMG=cybernetics-agentic-ui-api:$TAG
TAR=agentic-ui-api-$TAG.tar

# 1. Stream to the server (verify the checksum matches on both sides)
docker save "$IMG" | tee >(sha256sum) | ssh K3s-server "cat > ~/$TAR"
ssh K3s-server "sha256sum ~/$TAR"

# 2. Import into containerd — needs a sudo password, so this ssh gets -t
ssh -t K3s-server "sudo k3s ctr -n k8s.io images import ~/$TAR"

# 3. Confirm the node sees the tag before rolling out
ssh K3s-server 'kubectl get node -o json | grep -o "cybernetics-agentic-ui-api:[^\"]*" | sort -u'

# 4. Roll out and record why
ssh K3s-server "kubectl -n librechat set image deploy/librechat librechat=$IMG"
ssh K3s-server "kubectl -n librechat annotate deploy/librechat kubernetes.io/change-cause='$TAG' --overwrite"
ssh K3s-server "kubectl -n librechat rollout status deploy/librechat --timeout=300s"

# 5. Clean up the staged tar
ssh K3s-server "rm ~/$TAR"
```

## Gotchas

- **Pipe, never `&&`.** `docker save` writes the tar to stdout. With `&&` the
  stream goes to your terminal instead, and Docker aborts with `cowardly
  refusing to save to a terminal` — so the whole chain short-circuits and
  nothing is transferred.
- **No `-t` on the streaming ssh.** A pty translates `\n` to `\r\n` and
  silently corrupts the tar. Only the sudo import needs `-t`.
- **No colons in the tar filename.** Legal on ext4, but `scp` reads `:` as the
  host/path separator, so such a path is unusable with scp.
- **Don't stage in `/tmp`** — it is tmpfs (RAM-backed, 7.7G) on a host with
  ~5Gi free. Use `~`, which sits on the 452G root volume.
- **Skip compression.** Docker uses the containerd image store, so `docker
  save` already emits compressed blobs (measured zstd ratio: 1.00x).
- **Never run `kubectl apply -k ~/dev-ops/k3s-deployment/apps/librechat/`.**
  That manifest has drifted: it still points at
  `registry.librechat.ai/danny-avila/librechat-dev:latest` with no
  `imagePullPolicy`, and its ConfigMap has 13 keys against ~100+ live. An
  apply reverts the image and guts the live config. Use `kubectl set image`.
- **Rollback needs no transfer** — the previous image stays in containerd:
  `kubectl -n librechat rollout undo deploy/librechat`.

## Notes

- `strategy: Recreate` with 1 replica: the old pod dies before the new one
  starts, so expect 30-40s of downtime. `startupProbe` allows up to 300s.
- Verify with a *new-build* asset, not just `/health` — a healthy pod proves
  nothing about which build is serving.
